# This file cites the software: the repository, its code and its results snapshot.
# The title names the project rather than a paper. Once the paper has an arXiv
# identifier, add a `preferred-citation` block here pointing at the paper, so that a
# citation of this work resolves to the paper and this entry stays the software record.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Recovering Latent Compression: Sandhi-Aware, Morpheme-Constrained Tokenization for Sanskrit Language Modelling"
abstract: >-
  Sanskrit is information-dense per word, but subword tokenizers are trained on
  raw sandhied, compounded text. This repository tests whether that density
  survives tokenization when measured per unit of meaning rather than per word,
  and whether reversing sandhi before subword learning and forbidding merges
  across gold morpheme boundaries recovers it. Headline metrics are
  tokens-per-proposition on parallel text and bits-per-character from language
  model training; fertility is always computed and never led with.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Devansh
repository-code: "https://github.com/DS436/sanskrit-token"
url: "https://github.com/DS436/sanskrit-token"
license: MIT
keywords:
